/-!
# Checked steps of the genuine 14.7 local endgame

The chief-factor step now lifts the displacement bound to the original
finite group: the genuine C-component and the original star map give
[K,C_H(U)] ≤ U, with no elementary-section or descended-action assumption.
The chosen even involution is constructed in the order-two image of Uα.

The rank-two U₀ exclusion constructs the original R-action through the
marked L/O₂(L), using R ≤ C_G(Q). An index-at-most-two subgroup of the
actual Sylow image fixes a vector outside V, forcing R = V × C_R(L).
The original 14.7.68(2) then proves U₀ = V₁, conditional on the still-needed
generation identities for R. Neither R ≤ L nor U₀ ≤ L is assumed.

For the later P/U section, the original conjugate roots and their Frattini
bounds make E/U central and P/U elementary. A genuine Sylow SP in the
perfect group K then proves [P,K]U=P by the central-cover obstruction.
The canonical representation on the literal P/U quotient descends through
H/P≃S₅. Its projection to the original natural P/E coordinates has fixed
kernel E/U. Transport supplies module commutator generation; with |E/U|=4,
the same section is identified with the universal natural cover and gives
the literal six-dimensional indecomposable fields of RuTwo.

The same original qL now supplies the natural Ru1 section and the
conditional Steinberg transport. Characteristic two and the actual natural
Sylow fixed line prove Z(T)=V₁ once T≤L is known. After U₀=V₁, the original
projection is injective and gives the full S₅ natural Ru2 section on the
literal H=C_G(Z(T)) and U=⟨Vᴴ⟩.

These are conditional steps inside 14.7.71–74. Full chief-factor placement,
the generation identities for R, Steinberg recognition and special-group
equalities, marked natural P/E recognition, Sylow SP, the order-four
fixed-kernel count, M=L and O₂(H)=O₂(K) remain source obligations.
Final 71–74 assembly remains with this local endgame; qt-14-07 retains the
earlier-source discharge and final 14.7.75 recognition.

Source: Aschbacher–Smith, combined manuscript of 1 March 2004,
14.7.71–75, printed pp.1075–1078 (PDF pp.1092–1095).
-/
